...@classes

direction: down

title: Headless lifeline - route-metric failover {
  near: top-center
  shape: text
  style: {font-color: "#727169"; font-size: 20; bold: true}
}

cwwk: CWWK S8 (router) {class: ours}

wan: WAN via WAS-110\nmetric 100 {class: box}
tether: Android USB tether\ncdc_ncm / rndis_host\nmetric 2048 {class: box}

net: Internet {class: carrier}
ygg: Yggdrasil mesh\n(SSH + mosh on ygg0) {class: ours}

cwwk -> wan: primary {style.stroke: "#98bb6c"}
cwwk -> tether: backup {style.stroke: "#e6c384"; style.stroke-dash: 3}
wan -> net: wins when fiber up {style.stroke: "#98bb6c"}
tether -> net: wins when fiber pulled {style.stroke: "#e6c384"; style.stroke-dash: 3}
net -> ygg
ygg -> cwwk: reachable regardless of path {style.stroke: "#7e9cd8"}

note: Metric 2048 only activates when the metric-100 route is gone.\nPull the fiber, Yggdrasil re-routes over mobile, SSH stays up. {
  near: bottom-center
  shape: text
  style: {font-color: "#e6c384"; font-size: 14; italic: true}
}
